-- title:
--   Four natural-number sensitivity profile bounds
-- statement:
--   A profile-bound vector is a tuple
--   $$v=(s_0,s_1,j_0,j_1)\in\mathbb N^4.$$
--   The fields are intended to majorize zero-side sensitivity, one-side sensitivity, zero-side joint sensitivity and one-side joint sensitivity, respectively. Side sensitivity is maximized over a nested family of total Boolean predicates and inputs where the chosen predicate has the indicated output. Joint sensitivity counts raw coordinates whose single flip changes two distinct ordered predicates at the same input, both with that output, and is maximized over such pairs and inputs.
--
--   This bundle defines only the data structure `RawBounds`; it asserts no bound on a function. Keeping the four coordinates separate permits later componentwise induction without collapsing the two joint profiles.
-- source:
